<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alessandro Manzoni</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1785">1785</a>–<a href="/years/1873">1873</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alessandro Manzoni was an Italian novelist and poet from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>. His historical novel The Betrothed (I promessi sposi), set in Spanish-ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombardy">Lombardy</a> in 1628–1630 and describing the plague of 1630, appeared in its final form in 1840–1842 and became a founding work of modern Italian literature and language. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giuseppe-verdi">Giuseppe Verdi</a> composed his Requiem in Manzoni's memory.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alessandro-manzoni.jpg" alt="Alessandro Manzoni" width="320" height="422" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Francesco Hayez · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Francesco_Hayez_-_Ritratto_di_Alessandro_Manzoni.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Heavy taxation, troop billeting and the plague of 1630, which killed perhaps half the population of the city and is the setting of <b>Alessandro Manzoni</b>’s novel The Betrothed, weakened Lombardy in the seventeenth century.</blockquote><a href="/empire/duchy-of-milan">Duchy of Milan · Decline &amp; Fall</a></li><li><blockquote>Elsewhere Alexander Pushkin in Russia, Adam Mickiewicz in Lithuania and later in exile, <b>Alessandro Manzoni</b> in Milan with his novel The Betrothed, and Ralph Waldo Emerson and the Transcendentalists in New England gave the movement national forms.</blockquote><a href="/movement/romanticism">Romanticism · People</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/milan">Milan</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/italy">Italy</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=45.47,9.19&amp;year=1842" aria-label="Milan on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4768 560 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Alessandro Manzoni"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5218 830h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5218 830h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=45.47,9.19&amp;year=1842">What was here in 1842? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
